<title>USA: ARV adopts shareholder rights plan.</title>
<headline>ARV adopts shareholder rights plan.</headline>
<dateline>COSTA MESA, Calif. 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>ARV Assisted Living Inc Tuesday said it has adopted a shareholders rights plan that is triggered if a person or group acquires or makes a tender offer for 10 percent or more of the company's stock.</p>
<p>Under the plan each right distributed to shareholders, when excercised, entitles its holder to purchase common shares with a market value at least twice the rights' exercisable price.</p>
<p>Earlier, ARV announced the sale of 9.6 million shares to an affiliate of Lazard Freres Real Estate Investors LLC. Shares owned by it and ARV Chief Executive Officer Gary Davidson are exempt from the plan.</p>
</text>
